  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Evaluate the following statements for their correctness.</p><p>A. The elevation in boiling point temperature of water will be same for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaCl</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> urea.<br />B. Azeotropic mixture boil without change in their composition.<br />C. Osmosis always takes place from hypertonic to hypotonic solution.<br />D. The density of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>32</mn><mo>%</mo></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> solution having molarity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>09</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> is approximately <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>26</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mL</mi><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>.<br />E. A negatively charged sol is obtained when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>KI</mi></math> solution is added to silver nitrate solution.</p><p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "O3cGm",
      "text": "B and D only",
      "isCorrect": true,
