  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>(A) Elevation in boiling point (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></msub></math>)&nbsp;temperature of the water is not same, as &lsquo;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></math>&rsquo; value is different for two solutions.<br />(B) Azeotropic mixture: Liquid mixtures that distill over without changes in composition are called constant boiling mixtures or Azeotropes or Azeotropic mixtures.<br />(C) Osmosis always takes place from hypotonic (low concentration of solute) solution to hypertonic (high concentration of solute) solution.<br />(D)&nbsp;Let the mass of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;(<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>32</mn><mo>%</mo></math>) is 100.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>&nbsp;Weight of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;=&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>32</mn></math></p><p>Moles of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mn>32</mn><mn>98</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Now,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>09</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mn>32</mn><mrow><mn>98</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>79</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math></p><p>Density =&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>100</mn><mn>79</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>265</mn></math><br />(E) A negative charged sol&nbsp;is obtained when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>KI</mi></math> solution is added to silver nitrate solution whereas positive charged sol&nbsp;is obtained when&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>AgNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;solution is added to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>KI</mi></math>&nbsp;solution.</p><p>So, the correct answer is B and D only.</p>",
